-- allium: 3
--
-- Lapse — a player whose marks fall behind, who guesses, and who is wrong
--
-- Scope
--   The third of three models of a player, and the one in which a limit
--   leads to error. The player's marks are kept up only as far as their
--   upkeep reaches, so they fall behind the grid; a look that finds nothing
--   is answered by checking them, and when patience runs out by a guess; a
--   guess can be wrong, and a wrong one is found out and put right. A puzzle
--   is rated by how many steps all of that takes. reach.allium and
--   effort.allium model the same player differently and none of the three
--   imports another.
--   This module is coarse. Its lifecycle and the four kinds of step are
--   stated; how a guess is chosen, how well a player restores a grid and
--   whether every run ends are open questions, and nothing should be built
--   on them yet.
--   Source: docs/explanation/solving-sudoku.md, for hand backtracking: a
--   checkpoint, a branch, and a return to the checkpoint on contradiction.
--
-- Includes
--   - Where error comes from, which is not where it first seems. By
--     technique.allium's ExtraCandidatesHideAndNeverMislead, marks that have
--     fallen behind allow too much and so hide deductions; they never
--     license a false one. A deterministic player is therefore wrong only by
--     guessing. Lapsed marks are what bring the guess on.
--   - Upkeep: after a placement the digit is struck from the marks of the
--     peers the profile's upkeep reaches, and from no others.
--   - Four kinds of step: a deduction, a check of the marks, a guess and a
--     repair.
--   - The run, which ends solved, or abandoned where it is in contradiction
--     with no guess to blame or has nothing left to guess.
--
-- Excludes
--   - Slips: a digit misread, a candidate struck by mistake, a mark never
--     written. They need chance, which this game reaches through its
--     randomness port, and they are the layer this model is built to take
--     later. Nothing here is drawn at random.
--   - Cost, which is effort.allium's, and hints, which are reach.allium's. A
--     mistaken belief is never offered as a hint. So this model reads
--     repertoire, capacity, spans, marking, order, fixation, upkeep and
--     patience, and ignores budget and fatigue.
--   - Which of several equal deductions or guesses is taken.
--
-- Dependencies
--   sudoku.allium, for Given, and technique.allium, for the grid, the
--   catalogue, deductions, placements and the profile.
--
-- Vocabulary
--   technique.allium's words stand, and solver.allium's guess: never trial,
--   never bifurcation. To them: run, look and step, as in reach.allium, each
--   module's own. Lapsed, of marks that still allow what a placed peer rules
--   out; technique.allium calls the candidate stale. Check, a step that
--   brings every mark up to date. Standing, of a guess not yet withdrawn.
--   Repair, the return to the grid as it stood before a guess, with the
--   guessed digit struck.

use "./sudoku.allium" as sudoku
use "./technique.allium" as technique

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

enum StepKind { deduction | check | guess | repair }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

entity Run {
    profile: technique/Profile
    start: Set<sudoku/Given>
    status: looking | stepping | solved | abandoned

    transitions status {
        looking -> stepping
        stepping -> looking
        looking -> solved
        looking -> abandoned
        terminal: solved, abandoned
    }

    -- The player's grid: their digits and their marks. There is no second
    -- grid holding the truth, because the player has none to look at; what a
    -- rating knows beyond the player is read from the solution.
    grid: technique/Grid with keeper = this

    steps: Step with run = this
    last_steps: steps where is_last
    standing_guesses: steps where is_standing_guess
    latest_standing_guesses: steps where is_latest_standing_guess

    -- Looks in a row that found nothing. A deduction sets it back to none.
    fruitless_looks: Integer

    sees(x):
        profile.knows(x) and profile.holds(x)
            and profile.takes_in(x) and profile.can_read(x)

    sees_something: grid.deductions.any(x => sees(x))

    -- How a wrong guess shows itself to the player: two peers holding one
    -- digit, which is a placed cell whose own digit has gone stale, or an
    -- open cell with no mark left.
    is_in_contradiction:
        grid.is_contradictory
            or grid.cells.any(c => c.digit != null and c.has_stale_candidate)

    has_cell_to_guess: grid.open_cells.any(c => c.candidates.count >= config.fewest_to_guess)

    -- Ready to look. A grid is born kept, by technique.allium's
    -- AGridIsBornKept, so the first marking-up is true; after that a run
    -- looks at its marks as they are, lapsed or not.
    is_poised: status = looking and grid != null and grid.is_laid_out
}

entity Step {
    run: Run
    index: Integer
    kind: StepKind

    -- Present on a deduction step, and the placement on a guess.
    deduction: technique/Deduction?
    guessed: technique/Placement?

    -- A guess a repair has taken back.
    is_withdrawn: Boolean

    is_last: run.steps.all(o => o.index <= index)
    is_standing_guess: kind = guess and not is_withdrawn
    is_latest_standing_guess:
        is_standing_guess
            and run.steps.all(o => o.is_standing_guess implies o.index <= index)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    side: Integer = sudoku/config.side

    -- A guess is between alternatives, so on a cell with at least two marks.
    fewest_to_guess: Integer = 2
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

rule BeginRun {
    when: Attempt(givens, profile)

    requires: solution_count(givens, config.side) = 1

    ensures: Run.created(
        profile: profile,
        start: givens,
        status: looking,
        fruitless_looks: 0
    )
}

rule OpenGrid {
    when: run: Run.created

    ensures: technique/Grid.created(keeper: run, start: run.start)
}

rule Look {
    when: run: Run.is_poised

    requires: run.status = looking
    requires: run.is_poised

    -- Read before anything changes: the count of looks is compared as it
    -- stood, and the step about to be recorded is not among the steps.
    let is_patient = run.fruitless_looks < run.profile.patience
    let next_index = run.steps.count + 1

    -- One rule and its ends, in this order. A contradiction is repaired if a
    -- guess stands to blame, and otherwise the run is abandoned. A full grid
    -- with no contradiction is solved. Something seen is taken, as in
    -- reach.allium. Nothing seen is a fruitless look: within patience the
    -- player checks their marks, which may uncover what lapsed marks hid;
    -- past it they guess, if any cell offers a choice. guess_for is a black
    -- box: the placement this player would try, on their marks.
    ensures:
        if run.is_in_contradiction and run.standing_guesses.count = 0:
            run.status = abandoned
        else if run.is_in_contradiction:
            Step.created(run: run, index: next_index, kind: repair, is_withdrawn: false)
            run.status = stepping
        else if run.grid.is_filled:
            run.status = solved
        else if run.sees_something:
            Step.created(
                run: run,
                index: next_index,
                kind: deduction,
                deduction: chosen(filter(run.grid.deductions, x => run.sees(x))),
                is_withdrawn: false
            )
            run.fruitless_looks = 0
            run.status = stepping
        else if is_patient:
            Step.created(run: run, index: next_index, kind: check, is_withdrawn: false)
            run.fruitless_looks = run.fruitless_looks + 1
            run.status = stepping
        else if run.has_cell_to_guess:
            Step.created(
                run: run,
                index: next_index,
                kind: guess,
                guessed: guess_for(run.grid, run.profile),
                is_withdrawn: false
            )
            run.fruitless_looks = 0
            run.status = stepping
        else:
            run.status = abandoned
}

rule TakeStep {
    when: run: Run.status transitions_to stepping

    requires: run.status = stepping

    -- The guess a repair blames, read before the repair withdraws it.
    let blamed_guesses = run.latest_standing_guesses

    -- By kind. A deduction's strikes are taken as in reach.allium. A
    -- placement, deduced or guessed, goes in its cell and leaves the marks
    -- of those open peers that share with it a unit of a kind the player
    -- keeps up, and of no others: that is the lapse. A check strikes every
    -- stale mark. A repair takes the latest standing guess back: every cell
    -- is as it stood before that guess, and the guessed digit is struck from
    -- the guessed cell. digit_before and candidates_before are black boxes:
    -- the cell as it stood when that step was recorded.
    ensures:
        run.status = looking
        for step in run.last_steps:
            let placed = if step.kind = guess: step.guessed else: step.deduction?.placement
            if step.kind = deduction:
                for strike in step.deduction.strikes:
                    for cell in run.grid.cells:
                        if cell.row = strike.position.row and cell.column = strike.position.column:
                            cell.candidates = cell.candidates - strike.digits
            if placed != null:
                for cell in run.grid.cells:
                    if cell.row = placed.position.row and cell.column = placed.position.column:
                        cell.digit = placed.digit
                        cell.candidates = { placed.digit }
                        for peer in cell.peers:
                            if peer.digit = null
                                    and ((row in run.profile.upkeep and peer.row = cell.row)
                                        or (column in run.profile.upkeep and peer.column = cell.column)
                                        or (box in run.profile.upkeep
                                            and peer.box_number = cell.box_number)):
                                peer.candidates = peer.candidates - { placed.digit }
            if step.kind = check:
                for cell in run.grid.stale_cells:
                    cell.candidates = cell.candidates - cell.placed_peer_digits
            if step.kind = repair:
                for blamed in blamed_guesses:
                    blamed.is_withdrawn = true
                    for cell in run.grid.cells:
                        cell.digit = digit_before(blamed, cell)
                        if cell.row = blamed.guessed.position.row
                                and cell.column = blamed.guessed.position.column:
                            cell.candidates = candidates_before(blamed, cell) - { blamed.guessed.digit }
                        else:
                            cell.candidates = candidates_before(blamed, cell)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant StepsCarryWhatTheirKindNeeds {
    for step in Steps:
        (step.kind = deduction implies step.deduction != null)
            and (step.kind = guess implies step.guessed != null)
            and (step.is_withdrawn implies step.kind = guess)
}

invariant EveryDeductionStepWasSeen {
    for step in Steps:
        step.kind = deduction implies step.run.sees(step.deduction)
}

invariant SolvedMeansFilledAndConsistent {
    for run in Runs:
        run.status = solved implies run.grid.is_filled and not run.is_in_contradiction
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

surface Attempting {
    provides:
        Attempt(givens, profile)

    @guarantee OnlyAGuessIsEverWrong
        -- A grid is born kept, upkeep and checks strike only what a placed
        -- peer rules out, and a deduction read from marks that allow
        -- too much is sound. So while no guess stands, every digit in the
        -- grid is the solution's. A solved run's grid is the solution, since
        -- a full grid with no contradiction is one and the puzzle has one.

    @guarantee SameInputSameRun
        -- The same givens and the same profile give the same steps, the
        -- same guesses and the same end, every time.
}

surface AttemptResult {
    context run: Run

    exposes:
        run.status
        run.profile
        run.steps.count
        run.standing_guesses.count
        for step in run.steps:
            step.index
            step.kind
            step.deduction
            step.guessed
            step.is_withdrawn
            step.is_last
            step.is_latest_standing_guess
        for cell in run.grid.cells:
            cell.row
            cell.column
            cell.digit
            cell.candidates
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "guess_for: which cell and which digit. solver.allium guesses on a cell with the fewest candidates; does a person, on their marks, and does a player with no marks guess by sight?"

open question "Does every run end? A repair strikes the guessed digit, as solver.allium's split does, which suggests it does; but checks and guesses alternate here and it has not been shown."

open question "Repair restores the grid perfectly. The source asks a careful solver to keep a clean snapshot; does a novice, or do they erase what they remember and leave the rest?"

open question "A contradiction is seen the moment it stands. With lapsed marks a conflict can sit unnoticed; should noticing be bounded by spans as seeing a deduction is?"

open question "Does a check bring every mark up to date, or only those the player's spans take in, and should a player with no marks check at all? As stated one check leaves nothing stale, so every later fruitless look before the guess changes nothing and only counts."

open question "The stochastic layer: slip rates for a misread digit, a mark wrongly struck and a mark never written, drawn through the randomness port and reproducible by seed. Which of them, and on which profile fields?"

open question "Should steps be the only measure, or should a run also report guesses made, guesses withdrawn and checks, which a rating could weigh differently?"
